{% comment %}
  Cartel email popup — 10%-off newsletter capture (lane 7C), rendered on
  every page from theme.liquid, hidden until cartel-conversion.js opens it
  (auto once per visitor via localStorage "cl_popup", or from the offer tab).
  Every string and the image half are merchant-editable from Theme settings ->
  Email popup; each falls back to the string it was hardcoded to, so a cleared
  field can never paint an empty popup. With no image set, the branded CL
  monogram panel renders exactly as it did before the setting existed. Signup =
  Dawn's newsletter pattern: {% form 'customer' %} + hidden
  contact[tags]=newsletter. After a successful post the page reloads and
  [data-popup-posted] tells the JS to reopen once with the success state.
  Skin: assets/cartel-conversion.css.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="cl cl-fixed">
  <div class="ov" id="cl-popup-ov" hidden>
    <div class="pop" id="cl-popup" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Get 10% off your first order">
      <button class="pop-close" type="button" data-popup-close aria-label="Close">
        <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5.5 5.5l13 13M18.5 5.5l-13 13"></path></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="pop-img">
        {%- comment -%}
          The panel is half the 900px popup on desktop and full-bleed but only
          200px tall on mobile, so the crop is severe: honour the focal point
          the merchant set on the file. alt is left to image_tag, which reads
          the file's own alt text and emits alt="" (correctly decorative, like
          the monogram panel it replaces) when there is none.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if settings.popup_image != blank -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign pop_focal = settings.popup_image.presentation.focal_point
            assign pop_img_style = ''
            if pop_focal
              assign pop_img_style = 'object-position:' | append: pop_focal
            endif
          -%}
          {{
            settings.popup_image
            | image_url: width: 900
            | image_tag:
              widths: '300,450,600,900',
              sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 450px, 94vw',
              loading: 'lazy',
              style: pop_img_style
          }}
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="pop-img-brand" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="pop-monogram">CL</span>
            <span class="pop-monogram-sub">Cartel Lash Supply</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Fix 2026-08-10. This used to render the success arm OR the form arm off
        form.posted_successfully?, which is scoped to the request's form_type and
        not to a form id — so a failed footer signup painted this popup's error
        and prefilled the rejected address, and a successful one replaced the
        whole popup with "You're in." before the visitor had typed anything.
        Both halves now render (the form half hidden when a post happened), each
        tagged with the form id, exactly like the newsletter bands in
        main-article / main-blog / cartel-email; cartel-conversion.js keeps the
        half whose id matches the redirect fragment. With JS off this degrades to
        the previous behaviour.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- form 'customer', id: 'cl-popup-form', class: 'pop-b' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Fix 2026-08-30. This assign used to sit ABOVE the {%- form -%} tag,
          where `form` does not exist yet — it is only defined inside a
          {% form %} block — so form.posted_successfully? was always nil,
          pop_hide was always '' and .pop-offer below never got its `hidden`
          class. Someone who had just subscribed saw "You're in. / Your welcome
          code is on its way" with the "Take 10% off your first order" pitch, an
          empty email field and a Claim button stacked directly beneath it.
          Moved inside the block, exactly like cartel-email.liquid:29-33.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign pop_hide = '' -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          {%- assign pop_hide = ' hidden' -%}
          <div class="pop-done-wrap" data-popup-posted data-cl-form-ok="cl-popup-form">
            <div class="pop-done-ic">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <h2 class="pop-h">{{ settings.popup_success_heading | default: "You're in." }}</h2>
            <p class="pop-p">
              {{- settings.popup_success_body | default: "Your welcome code is on its way to your inbox. Welcome to the Cartel." -}}
            </p>
            <button class="btn btn-fill" type="button" data-popup-close>
              {{- settings.popup_success_button | default: 'Start shopping' -}}
            </button>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="pop-offer{{ pop_hide }}" data-cl-form-fields="cl-popup-form">
          <span class="kick">{{ settings.popup_kicker | default: 'First order treat' }}</span>
          <h2 class="pop-h">{{ settings.popup_heading | default: 'Take 10% off your first order.' }}</h2>
          <p class="pop-p">
            {{- settings.popup_body | default: 'Join the Cartel list for pro tips, restock alerts and early access to drops.' -}}
          </p>
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter">
          <div class="pop-form">
            <input
              class="pop-input"
              type="email"
              name="contact[email]"
              value="{{ form.email }}"
              data-cl-form-email="cl-popup-form"
              required
              placeholder="{{ settings.popup_placeholder | default: 'Your email address' | escape }}"
              aria-label="Email address"
              autocomplete="email"
              autocapitalize="off"
              autocorrect="off"
            >
            <button class="btn btn-fill w100" type="submit">
              {{- settings.popup_button | default: 'Claim my 10%' -}}
            </button>
          </div>
          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <div class="pop-msg-err" role="alert" data-popup-error data-cl-form-msg="cl-popup-form">
              Hmm, that email doesn't look right. Try again?
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          <button class="pop-skip" type="button" data-popup-close>
            {{- settings.popup_skip | default: "No thanks, I'll pay full price" -}}
          </button>
        </div>
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
